WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.451
Exercise 2: data contract evolution.

2
00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:14.068
The orders team adds a quantity column in the new schema orders_v2.

3
00:00:14.118 --> 00:00:21.036
Start v2 as a copy of the v1 contract.

4
00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:23.538
Open the copy in the editor. It still says orders_v1.

5
00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:27.558
New major version: ID orders_v2, version 2.0.0.

6
00:00:27.608 --> 00:00:31.938
Point the server to the orders_v2 schema.

7
00:00:31.988 --> 00:00:42.658
Add the new quantity property to line_items.

8
00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:57.984
Add a quality rule: quantity must be greater than 0.

9
00:00:58.034 --> 00:01:12.455
Save, then run the tests against orders_v2.

10
00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:25.796
The editor wrote everything to the YAML file.

11
00:01:25.846 --> 00:01:35.593
datacontract changelog lists every difference between v1 and v2.

12
00:01:35.643 --> 00:01:46.704
datacontract breaking rates each change. Adding a column is not breaking for the tool.

13
00:01:46.754 --> 00:02:01.545
Changing a type is breaking: ERROR and exit code 1.

14
00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:11.253
New in ODCS 3.2: mark a field deprecated first. That is only INFO.

15
00:02:11.303 --> 00:02:18.408
Lifecycle: draft, active, deprecated, retired. Set v1 to deprecated with an end of support date.

16
00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:25.759
Release v2 as active and retire v1. Done.
